// fun.marco — the "fun" globals from MacroMarco: dice roller, Magic 8-Ball, and
// fantasy name generator. These need randomness, which the OS act provides as
// host primitives (Roll / EightBall / Name) — a clean example of the host
// supplying capability Marco's pure runtime lacks.
//
// Randomness only works under a real host; run with --host windows:
//   bridges\ahk-hotkeys.ahk | marco serve --host windows programs/fun.marco
//   ...then events: {"feed":"Hotkeys","event":"Roll"}  {"event":"EightBall"} {"event":"Name"}
//
// (Under --host dryrun the host calls log and return no value, so the results
// are blank — these commands are meant for a live host.)

use os.

the Hotkeys is a feed of any.

// A dice-roll range.
the Range is a set.
this's Min is a number.
this's Max is a number.

the Fun is an actor.

// `r` — roll a number in 1..20.
this can Roll.
this's Roll does...
    the range is a Range with Min 1, Max 20.
    do OS's Roll with range...
        when ok?
            log that.
            this is ok!
        or?
            this is failed with that's error!

// `8` — Magic 8-Ball answer.
this can EightBall.
this's EightBall does...
    do OS's EightBall...
        when ok?
            log that.
            this is ok!
        or?
            this is failed with that's error!

// `n` — random fantasy name.
this can Name.
this's Name does...
    do OS's Name...
        when ok?
            log that.
            this is ok!
        or?
            this is failed with that's error!

when Hotkeys reads Roll?
    do Fun's Roll...
        when ok?
            log "rolled".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads EightBall?
    do Fun's EightBall...
        when ok?
            log "8-ball".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads Name?
    do Fun's Name...
        when ok?
            log "name".
        or?
            log that's error.

the App is a script.
log "fun ready".
